WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.194
OT environments combine specialized control devices with familiar computing and networking technology.

00:00:06.194 --> 00:00:13.764
Understanding the role of each component helps analysts interpret traffic, ownership, exposure, and operational consequence.

00:00:13.764 --> 00:00:20.417
A programmable logic controller, or PLC, executes control logic close to the process.

00:00:20.417 --> 00:00:27.070
It reads inputs, applies programmed rules, and updates outputs on a predictable cycle.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:38.770
A remote terminal unit, or RTU, performs similar monitoring and control functions, often at geographically distributed locations such as pipelines, substations, or pumping stations.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:44.505
These devices may operate for long periods with limited local support.

00:00:44.505 --> 00:00:49.781
A human-machine interface, or HMI, gives operators visibility and control.

00:00:49.781 --> 00:00:59.646
It displays measurements, equipment state, alarms, and process graphics, and may allow authorized users to issue commands or adjust setpoints.

00:00:59.646 --> 00:01:12.722
A supervisory control and data acquisition system, commonly called SCADA, coordinates monitoring and supervisory control across a wider operation, often connecting central control functions with remote sites.

00:01:12.722 --> 00:01:20.293
Engineering workstations are used to configure controllers, develop logic, maintain device settings, and troubleshoot systems.

00:01:20.293 --> 00:01:25.110
Their privileges and software make them highly sensitive assets.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:30.846
Historians collect time-series process data for analysis, reporting, optimization, and investigation.

00:01:30.846 --> 00:01:38.875
Because historians frequently exchange data with business systems, they can sit near an important trust boundary.

00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:44.610
Sensors measure conditions such as temperature, pressure, flow, position, or speed.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:53.557
Actuators turn control decisions into physical action by moving valves, starting motors, operating breakers, or changing equipment position.

00:01:53.557 --> 00:02:01.586
Industrial networks carry data among these components using Ethernet, serial links, wireless systems, and specialized protocols.

00:02:01.586 --> 00:02:05.486
No component should be evaluated in isolation.

00:02:05.486 --> 00:02:14.433
A workstation may appear to be an ordinary Windows computer, but its engineering tools can alter a process.

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:18.792
A network switch may carry time-sensitive control traffic.

00:02:18.792 --> 00:02:28.197
Good security begins by documenting each asset's function, communication relationships, owner, and consequence if it becomes unavailable or untrustworthy.
